From 7aa28daf072a40cea0b4cb4129e8d2a374ca9e02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Ballestrini <russell@unturf.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] b43: AC-PHY: 2 and 3 spatial streams on core rev >= 40

HT MCS 8..23: TX STBC, multi-core power back-off, the TX core table,
the per-rate TX power offset word, and the aggregate length limit for
2+ stream frames: aggregates longer than ~20 MPDUs at 300 Mbit/s are
acknowledged but carry no usable data, brcmsmac's per-rate FIFO preload
limit bounds them (acphy_htnss, acphy_mimo_ampdu, acphy_mimo_ffpld).
---
